        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(vydra): apply request policy to media generation requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running Vydra media generation would not get their configured provider request policy applied when the generation service is reached through the shared Vydra HTTP path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Vydra submit/download flow now builds its HTTP resolver from the configured provider request policy, so custom headers, proxy dispatchers, and private-network policy are carried into the generated media requests. The change stays inside the Vydra shared request setup and does not change model parameters or result parsing.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution prepared for Alix-007.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators can rely on the same request policy they configured for the provider when Vydra generates images or videos, including controlled network routing and required outbound headers.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### 2026-07-13 controlled local Vydra-compatible HTTP proof\n\n- Exact PR head tested and pushed: `6ce5e81ba2383cf154254d6c02b1e5c597c29df3`.\n- Scope: controlled local Vydra-compatible HTTP endpoint on `127.0.0.1`, using real `global fetch` through the provider image/video paths. This is stronger than the earlier mocked-fetch proof, but it is not a live Vydra API call.\n- Added proof coverage:\n  - image flow: POST `/api/v1/models/grok-imagine`, GET `/api/v1/jobs/job-local-image`, GET `/generated/local-image.png`\n  - video flow: POST `/api/v1/models/veo3`, GET `/api/v1/jobs/job-local-video`, GET `/generated/local-video.mp4`\n  - both submit and poll requests carried the configured `X-Vydra-Policy` header, with `request.allowPrivateNetwork: true` and a local private endpoint base URL.\n  - both flows returned completed generated media through the provider helpers.\n- Commands run:\n\n  ```bash\n  pnpm install --frozen-lockfile\n  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/vydra/image-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/vydra/video-generation-provider.test.ts\n  pnpm exec oxfmt --write --threads=1 extensions/vydra/provider-test-helpers.test.ts extensions/vydra/image-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/vydra/video-generation-provider.test.ts\n  git diff --check\n  ```\n\n- Result:\n\n  ```text\n  Test Files  2 passed (2)\n  Tests  16 passed (16)\n  [test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 44.45s\n  Finished in 15ms on 3 files using 1 threads.\n  git diff --check passed\n  ```\n\n- Not tested / remaining review gap: no live Vydra account, external proxy, TLS route, or real generated Vydra media artifact was exercised. The new evidence is local representative HTTP behavior and should not be represented as live-provider proof.\n\n### Original focused regression proof\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/vydra/image-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/vydra/video-generation-provider.test.ts`\n- Result: 2 test files passed, 14 tests passed before the local HTTP harness was added.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD --`\n- Result: passed.\n",
